* ============================================================================
* workspace_session_state.dts -- v3 session-state capture (owner requirement
* 2026-08-11: "we need the cursor states and refresh relations"). A v3 save
* emits CURSOR <area> <physical-recno> per open area plus CURRENT <area>; the
* v3 loader applies them after AREA/REL restoration, the saved selection
* outranks normalization, and the final refresh slaves children to the
* RESTORED parents. PHYSICAL recno is the anchor (the GPS prior art: logical
* row derives from physical under the active order); GPS is the verifier.
* Old loaders skip the lines (tolerate-unknown; the KEY precedent).
*
* Proof shape: drive Sales_Orders to BOTTOM (SO 6) with the child slaved,
* save the SESSION as v3, tear down completely, reload -- then assert the
* parent is at SO 6 (not row 1) and the child re-slaved to it through the
* load's own refresh. RUNTIME-PROVEN 2026-08-11 (build 15:22:32) first try:
* "restored 43 area(s) and 58 relation(s) (+ 43 cursor(s))", GPS Area 21
* Physical Recno 6 / Logical Row 6, child at Recno 11.
*
* Run: DO workspace_session_state | regression: REGRESSION RUN WORKSPACE_SESSION
* Markers: SS_T1 (parent restored at BOTTOM), SS_T2 (child slaved after restore).
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

FORMULA "WS-SESSION-PROOF-BEGIN"

* --- environment-first: the cascade bundle roots ----------------------------
* AMENDED 2026-08-28. THIS LEG USED TO LOAD cascade_all, AND THAT IS WHY THIS
* SPEC COULD NOT BE BRACKETED: cascade_all.dtschema is a posture FILE in the
* PRODUCTION workspaces directory, absent once AIF-078 L2 redirects the
* WORKSPACES slot at a scratch root. It also made the spec depend on a mutable
* artifact nobody owns -- re-save cascade_all and this spec's meaning changes
* with nothing going red.
*
* THE FIXTURE HAD TO CARRY REAL STRUCTURE HERE, unlike the v3 and RAM specs.
* SS_T1/SS_T2 assert that a saved SESSION restores a cursor AND its relation
* slaving, so a two-table posture is not enough -- it needs a parent, a child,
* an ORDER TAG, and a live relation. cascade_all supplied those at AREA 21
* (CASCADE_Sales_Orders, tag SO_ID) and AREA 24 (CASCADE_SO_Lines, tag SO_ID),
* related on SO_ID. That pair is reproduced below in SANDBOX, at THE SAME AREA
* NUMBERS and on THE SAME KEY, so both markers keep their slots and their
* values and the PROOF is untouched.
*
* SIX PARENT ROWS SO 'BOTTOM' LANDS ON SO_ID 6, which is what the arms read.
* The tag is BUILT rather than dropped: SET ORDER is part of the session state
* under test, so a fixture without one would quietly stop exercising half the
* claim.
*
* GUARDS ADDED (SS_G1/SS_G2), which the spec did not have. WSL_G4/G5 exist
* because a FIXTURE failure once wore a VERB failure's clothes, and RS_G1
* because an arm reading an unchanged value cannot tell 'survived' from 'never
* worked'. If either guard reds, treat BOTH arms as UNPROVEN.
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
WORKSPACE CLOSE
ERASE SSPAR CONFIRM
ERASE SSCHI CONFIRM

SELECT 21
CREATE X64 SSPAR (SO_ID N(4,0), SLBL C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE SO_ID WITH 1
REPLACE SLBL WITH "SO_ONE"
APPEND
REPLACE SO_ID WITH 2
REPLACE SLBL WITH "SO_TWO"
APPEND
REPLACE SO_ID WITH 6
REPLACE SLBL WITH "SO_SIX"
INDEX ON SO_ID TAG SO_ID

SELECT 24
CREATE X64 SSCHI (SO_ID N(4,0), CLBL C(10))
APPEND
REPLACE SO_ID WITH 1
REPLACE CLBL WITH "LINE_ONE"
APPEND
REPLACE SO_ID WITH 2
REPLACE CLBL WITH "LINE_TWO"
APPEND
REPLACE SO_ID WITH 6
REPLACE CLBL WITH "LINE_SIX"
INDEX ON SO_ID TAG SO_ID

REL ADD SSPAR SSCHI ON SO_ID TO SO_ID

* THE 'SET ORDER TAG SO_ID' LINE THAT USED TO STAND HERE IS REMOVED, AND THAT
* IS A STATED COVERAGE LOSS RATHER THAN A TIDY-UP. Measured 2026-08-28: the
* fixture's INDEX ON writes SO_ID.inx (2INX) while SET ORDER TAG looks for a
* CDX under the INDEXES root, so the line printed
*     SET ORDER: file not found: ...\INDEXES\x64\SSPAR.cdx
* and did NOTHING. SS_G1 passed anyway because the rows are written so that
* PHYSICAL bottom is already SO_ID 6 -- which means the line was decorative and
* the spec had quietly stopped exercising SET ORDER restoration while still
* appearing to test it. A no-op line that looks like coverage is worse than an
* absent one, so it is gone and the gap is named: THIS SPEC NO LONGER PROVES
* THAT A SAVED SESSION RESTORES SET ORDER. Restoring that arm needs a real CDX
* in the fixture, which INDEX ON does not produce; it is its own piece of work.
SELECT SSPAR
BOTTOM
? "SS_G1_parent_fixture_at_bottom:" + (SO_ID = 6)
REL REFRESH
SELECT SSCHI
? "SS_G2_relation_live_before_the_save:" + (SO_ID = 6)

* --- take the session somewhere specific ------------------------------------
SELECT 21
BOTTOM
REL REFRESH

* --- save the SESSION, not just the schema ----------------------------------
WORKSPACE SAVE sess_regress MEMO V3
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- resurrection ------------------------------------------------------------
WORKSPACE LOAD sess_regress MEMO
GPS
? "SS_T1_parent_restored_at_bottom:" + (SO_ID = 6)
* CORRECTED 2026-08-28, SAME DAY, AFTER A FALSE GREEN. This addressed the table
* by SLOT, and the amendment above kept the old slot on the reasoning that the
* previous fixture held it there. THAT REASONING WAS VOID: R130 says a
* posture's AREA numbers are KEYS, NOT ADDRESSES, and the load prints so --
* tables land at slots 0..N-1. The old fixture only worked because mcc_x64
* restored THIRTEEN areas, so the high slot was coincidentally occupied. With a
* small posture the slot reaches NOTHING -- and the marker still printed .T.,
* because a marker over a closed area does not error, it PICKS A SIDE (see
* claude/FINDING_MARKER_OVER_A_CLOSED_AREA_PICKS_A_SIDE.md). ADDRESSING BY NAME
* SURVIVES RELOCATION, which is why workspace_memo and workspace_load_shortfall
* stayed sound through the same change.
SELECT SSCHI
? "SS_T2_child_slaved_after_restore:" + (SO_ID = 6)

FORMULA "WS-SESSION-PROOF-END"

* --- teardown: restore the x64 disk environment -----------------------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
DO x64
